OpenEmbedded/Yocto BSP layer for Toradex Easy Installer
-------------------------------------------------------

This layer is used to build the Toradex Easy Installer utility.
It provides a small distro called `tezi` along with image recipes
for the root file system and recipes for the Qt based UI.

Dependencies
------------

This layer is built on the master branches of:

- bitbake
- openembedded-core
- meta-openembedded
- meta-qt5
- meta-freescale
- meta-arm
- meta-ti
- meta-qcom
- meta-toradex-bsp

The exact layers, URIs and revisions are defined by the bitbake-setup
configurations in default-registry/configurations/.

Building
--------

This layer is a bitbake-setup registry for Tezi images. Get bitbake-setup
(`git clone https://git.openembedded.org/bitbake`) and run:

    ./bitbake/bin/bitbake-setup --setting default registry \
        'git://github.com/toradex/meta-toradex-tezi.git;protocol=https;branch=master;rev=master' \
        init

bitbake-setup asks for a configuration, the target machine and whether to
accept the FSL EULA. The only configuration is tezi-master: all layers,
qt-tezi and qt-tezictl track their branch heads. Builds are not
reproducible.

Contributing
------------

This layer is maintained by Toradex.

When creating a patch of the last commit, use

    git format-patch -s --subject-prefix='meta-toradex-tezi][<branch>][PATCH' -1

To send it to the community, use

    git send-email --to yocto-patches@toradex.com <generated patch>

